<font face="arial,tahoma,helvetica" size="-1">
<a name="problems"></a>
<b class="header">Download Problems?</b>
<br><br>
<b>Error Messages?</b><br>
If you get a "Cannot Find Server" or "Page cannot be displayed" error, it probably does NOT mean that the server is broken. It just means that it's overcrowded and you're getting turned away because there's no room for you.
<br><br>
What to do? You can either try one of the special "Xfer" servers (like FilePlanet Xfer 1), which lets you wait in line for an open slot, or you can sign up for <A HREF="http://redir.gamespy.com/redir.asp?u=http%3A//www.fileplanet.com/index.asp%3Fpage=whatisit&t=http%3A//www.fileplanet.com/index.asp%3Fpage=whatisit%26Download%20Problems%20what%20to%20do%20link">FilePlanet Personal Server</A>, which lets you skip the waits and start downloading immediately. <br><br>
<b>File Not Found?</b><br>
If you find that the file you're looking for turns up missing, try another server. If you still can't find it, shoot us a message at <A HREF="mailto:404@fileplanet.com">404@fileplanet.com</A> and we'll check it out.
<br><br>
<b>Too Slow?</b><br>
If your download speeds are too slow, try another one that's closer to you geographically. 
Or, sign up for <A HREF="http://redir.gamespy.com/redir.asp?u=http%3A//www.fileplanet.com/index.asp%3Fpage=whatisit&t=http%3A//www.fileplanet.com/index.asp%3Fpage=whatisit%26Download%20Problems%20Too%20Slow%20link">FilePlanet Personal Server</A>, which gives you access to special high-bandwidth express servers!
<br><br>
<b>Having other problems?</b><br>
Check out our <A HREF="http://www.fileplanet.com/index.asp?page=help">Help Page</A> for more FAQs.
</font>

